course: dictionary
lesson: 14630
title: Strong words: potent
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Potent means very strong and powerful in its effect. A potent medicine, poison or drink works strongly, even in a tiny amount.
explain: «A few drops of this potent medicine will ease your cough.» Only a few drops are needed because the medicine is so strong. Take medicine only as a grown-up tells you, because a potent one must be used with great care.
explain: Potent can also describe an idea, a symbol or an argument. «The red poppy is a potent symbol of remembrance.» A poppy is not a drink, but it moves people's hearts and minds. Ask yourself: what does the word tell me about the strength of the effect?
fact: Potent means very strong and powerful in its effect.
fact: Potent can describe a medicine, a poison, a drink, an idea, a symbol or an argument.
fact: A potent medicine or poison works even in tiny amounts, so it must be used with great care.
fact: «Potent» can also mean having a strong effect on people's minds, as in «a potent symbol».
fact: The noun is potency, which means how strong an effect is.
exercise: «The doctor said the medicine is very potent, so only one spoonful is needed.» What does potent mean here? | Very cold to touch | *Very strong in its effect | Very sweet to taste | Very old and dusty
exercise: «The flag is a potent symbol for the whole team.» What does potent suggest about the flag? | Heavy to lift | *Strong, with a deep effect on people | Bright blue and yellow | Weak and easily forgotten
exercise: Which word is the noun form of potent? | potent | *potency | potential | potted
test: «The witch stirred a potent potion in her cauldron, and the whole room turned green.» What does potent mean in this story? | Cold and watery | *Very strong and powerful in its effect | Very quiet and calm | Slow to cook
test: Which is a good way to check the meaning of potent in a sentence? | *Swap in a word like strong and see if the sentence still makes sense | Count the letters in the word | Read the sentence backwards | Skip the word and never look at it again
exam: «Only a drop of the potent medicine is needed, so keep the bottle out of reach.» What does the sentence tell you about potent? | Pale and watery | Very tasty and sweet | *Strong enough that only a tiny amount works | Old and cracked
